/E (This project implements a practical Cybersecurity framework for small businesses using pfSense and Suricata to detect and prevent network-based attacks. A virtual lab environment \(Kali Linux, Ubuntu, pfSense\) was used to simulate real-world threats such as network scanning and intrusion attempts. Suricata was configured with updated rule sets to monitor traffic, generate alerts, and automatically block malicious activity. The solution focuses on cost-effective security controls, including intrusion detection, traffic filtering, and threat mitigation, providing a scalable and efficient defense mechanism for small-scale business networks.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
